ac-introduction.para:
The  class consists of nine families:



     provides requirements for the developer's description of the
    life-cycle model used in the development, production, delivery and maintenance life-cycle
    of the TOE;



     provides requirements for the management of the configuration items;



     requires a minimum set of configuration items to be managed in the
    defined way;



     is concerned with the developer's physical, logical, procedural,
    personnel, and other security controls;



     provides requirements for the development tools and implementation
    standards used by the developer;



     provides requirements for the handling of security flaws;



     provides requirements for the procedures used for the delivery of the
    TOE to the downstream user. processes occurring during the development of the TOE are
    denoted rather as transfers, and are handled in the context of integration and acceptance
    procedures in other families of this class;



     is concerned with the generation of certain artefacts during the
    development process;



     is concerned with the integration of composition parts and a
    consistency check of delivery procedures.
